# Who gets asked to review what. Later rules win, so the catch-all comes first.
#
# NOTE: `main`'s protection sets "required approving reviews" to 0, because a
# single-maintainer repo cannot satisfy a review requirement — GitHub never
# lets a PR author approve their own PR. Turning on "Require review from Code
# Owners" while @mrdoodles is the only owner would deadlock every PR the same
# way. This file is for routing and provenance until there is a second owner.

*                       @mrdoodles

# The tool itself: copied verbatim onto users' PATH, so a mistake ships to
# everyone on the next release rather than failing in CI.
/amd                    @mrdoodles
/install.sh             @mrdoodles

# Release-critical. The RAW= line and the curl URL name the moving major tag;
# if they disagree with the tag, `curl | bash` installs the wrong version.
/.github/workflows/     @mrdoodles

# Ships to users' ~/.claude, so it changes how other people's agents behave.
/.claude/skills/agile-md/ @mrdoodles
